Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 11/01/2023]
1. Reaction Q value has changed by about 10 keV compared to 2010 evaluation.
2. 40Sc - 40K mirror state assignments from Hansper et al. 2000; assignments of resonances above 1 MeV energy are ambiguous.
3. Proton widths estimated using C2S values adopted from Endt 1977 or Fink and Schiffer 1974.  
4. Gamma-ray widths are estimated from the lifetimes of the bound mirror states (ENSDF), with an assumed uncertainty of a factor of 2.
5. Er = 925 keV: IMME predicts the (3-)_2 state near 1.45 MeV excitation; this level has not been observed yet in 40Sc; assumed 50 keV uncertainty in its energy.
6. Er = 245 keV: the 39K(d,p) angular distribution reveals a very small ell=1 component compared to a dominant ell=3 one; therefore, the uncertainty on the partial
   witdh is set to a factor of 3.
7. Direct capture S factor estimated from C2S values in Endt 1977; assumed uncertainty is a factor of 3 because the ell = 1 component of the transition to the
   first excited state is much smaller than the ell = 3 component.
